# Ben's Burger Bar, the pack in words (content-diner: diner-pack, 2026-11-08)

`packs/diner/pack.js` (pack version 3) on the ladder, in spec 8's format. It is the first restaurant and **the template
the other content agents copy**: every field below is in the file in this order, with a comment. The format is
`docs/api/pack-format.md`; the line `docs/api/line.md`; the script `docs/api/script.md`; sounds `docs/api/audio.md`;
the food `docs/api/world.md`. Before this pass the pack was the Burger Bar's own format (orderStyles, unlocks,
milestones, personas): it is at `docs/backup/packs/diner/pack.js.before` and, frozen for the diner-specific tests,
`tests/packs/diner-golden/`.

**Check it** (from the game folder):

```
BB_PACKS=diner node --test "tests/*.test.cjs"
node -e "console.table(require('./tests/bot.cjs').pressReport('diner'))"
node -e "const b=require('./tests/bot.cjs'); console.log(b.schema.validate(b.merge(require('./packs/diner/pack.js'))))"
```

## 1. At a glance

| | |
|---|---|
| id, name | `diner`, "Ben's Burger Bar" (court: "Burger Bar", bottom arm, slot 2, open at the start) |
| version | 3 (was 2: a saved shift from before the ladder is dropped; coins stay) |
| format | 3: the script covers every moment for every speaker (diner-script, 2026-11-08; section 12 and `diner-script.md`) |
| manager | `{ id: 'mitch', art: 'mitch-burger' }`: red diner shirt and paper hat |
| backdrops | `counter` (every pack's) and, by station, `grill`, `board`, `fryer`, `drinks` |
| courses | `['main', 'side', 'drink']`: a two-item order is a burger with a side or a drink, listed in that order |
| levels | `{}`: the engine's ladder unchanged (section 5) |
| help | one paragraph (section 13) |
| theme | all 24 tokens, today's colours; they are bb.css's defaults (section 14) |
| dropped | `orderStyles`, `grossRate`, `grossMax`, `recipes.*.unlock` and `.milestone`, `backdrops`, `poses` (the cast's default map is the same), `dailySpecialBonus`, and every persona field in `regulars` and `manager` (name, art, who, voice, tts, twin, short, exact, newest, tipScale, threeStarScale: now `packs/cast/cast.js`, merged by `BB.cast.merge`) |

## 2. The line: stations and steps

Every screen has at most 4 answers, plus Ticket and Pause. Station order in a recipe is the line's order.

| Station | backdrop | Steps, in order | redo | tool | sounds |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `grill` "Grill" | `grill` | Add `patty` (max 3) → Cook `patty` (stage set `patty`) | "Redo the Grill" | `spatula` | `{ cook: 'sizzle', done: 'flip' }` |
| `board` "Board" | `board` | builds on `plate`, `base: 'bun'`, `cap: 'bun'` (the buns go on by themselves); Add, one each: cheese, bacon, lettuce, tomato, pickles, onion, ketchup, mustard, mayo | "Redo the Toppings" | | (add: plop; sauces squirt, by `ingredients[ing].sauce`) |
| `fryer` "Fryer" | `fryer` | Pick `from: ['fries', 'rings']` → Cook (what the pick picked, set `fried`) → Add `salt` | "Redo the Fryer" | `fryerBasket` | `{ cook: 'fryer', add: 'salt' }` |
| `drinks` "Drinks" | `drinks` | builds on `cup`; Pick `of: 'size'` (Small, Medium, Large) → Add `ice` → Pick `of: 'flavour'` (the recipe's drink pick) | "Redo the Drink" | | `{ done: 'fountain' }` |

What the player hears (words.js, Simple; Timed changes only the cook step):

- Grill: "Grill. Add a patty?" Add / Skip; then "Add a second patty?" Add / Done ("Done, one patty"), up to a third.
  Cook: "How done?" Rare / Medium / Medium Well / Well Done. Timed: "Take it off when it is right.", one button
  **Take It Off** (said "Take it off. Medium").
- Board: "Board. Cheese." Add / Skip ("Add cheese", "Skip cheese"), then "Bacon." and so on. A bad one adds Swap It
  ("Add the green cheese").
- Fryer: "Fryer. Fries and Onion Rings?" Fries / Onion Rings (words.js joins a `from` pick with "and"; asked of its
  owner as "or"). Cook: "How crispy?" Golden / Crispy / Extra Crispy. Timed: "Lift the basket when it is right.",
  button **Lift the Basket**. Then "Salt." Add / Skip.
- Drinks: "Drinks. What size?" Small / Medium / Large. "Ice." Add / Skip. "Which one?" Cola / Lemon-Lime / Orange Soda,
  or Lemonade / Iced Tea.
- Review: "Here it is." Ring It Up, the redo words, or Redo… (a row) when there are more than three.

## 3. Cooking: the stage sets

| set | stages (first .. last) | Simple `choose` | ask | stop | speed |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `patty` | raw, rare, medium, mediumWell, well, charred | Rare, Medium, Medium Well, Well Done | "How done?" | "Take It Off" | pack `cookSpeeds` 12 / 8 / 5 s, `wantedScale` 2 |
| `fried` | raw, golden, crispy, extraCrispy, burnt | Golden, Crispy, Extra Crispy | "How crispy?" | "Lift the Basket" | the same |

Stage names: Raw, Rare, Medium, Medium Well, Well Done, Charred, Golden, Crispy, Extra Crispy, Burnt. Charred and
Burnt are Timed's last stages (food left on stops there, one mistake), never gross-outs. The speeds are exactly the
spec's minimum; no set uses `simple: 'auto'`.

## 4. Recipes

`level` is the only gate (a level-n shift offers every recipe of level n or below). Prices are tips' base: price ×
(0.6 + 0.2 × stars). Ticket wording is as written (change 0, the normal picks).

| id | Name | level | course | stations | price | As written (the ticket) | Can change |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `hamburger` | Hamburger | 1 | main | grill, board | 6 | one patty, medium, with lettuce, tomato, pickles and ketchup | doneness; holds lettuce, tomato, pickles, ketchup; adds onion, mustard, mayo |
| `cheeseburger` | Cheeseburger | 1 | main | grill, board | 7 | one patty, medium, with cheese, lettuce, tomato, pickles and ketchup | as the hamburger |
| `baconCheeseburger` | Bacon Cheeseburger | 2 | main | grill, board | 9 | one patty, medium, with cheese, bacon, lettuce, tomato, onion and ketchup | holds lettuce, tomato, onion, ketchup; adds pickles, mustard, mayo |
| `doubleCheeseburger` | Double Cheeseburger | 2 | main | grill, board | 10 | two patties, medium, with cheese, lettuce, pickles, onion, ketchup and mustard | holds lettuce, pickles, onion, ketchup, mustard; adds tomato, mayo |
| `fries` | Fries | 2 | side | fryer | 3 | Fries: golden, with salt | fry (golden, crispy; extra crispy at level 5); holds salt |
| `onionRings` | Onion Rings | 2 | side | fryer | 4 | Onion Rings: golden, with salt | as fries |
| `fountain` | Fountain Drink (named by its drink) | 3 | drink | drinks | 2 | "Medium cola: with ice." | size; cola, lemon-lime or orange soda; holds ice |
| `lemonade` | Lemonade or Iced Tea (named by its drink) | 3 | drink | drinks | 3 | "Medium lemonade: with ice." | size; lemonade or iced tea; holds ice |
| `tower` | The Diner Tower (rare) | 4 | main | grill, board | 14 | three patties, medium, with cheese, bacon, lettuce, tomato, pickles, onion, ketchup, mustard and mayo | doneness; holds lettuce, tomato, pickles, onion or a sauce |
| `teamStack` | The Team Stack | `'event'` | main | grill, board | 20 | three patties, medium (the finale sets well done), with cheese, pickles, onion, ketchup and mustard; `look: { giant: true }` | the event's finale only |

Picks: `doneness` (rare, medium, mediumWell, well; normal medium), `fry` (golden, crispy; fancy adds extraCrispy;
normal golden), `cupSize` (small, medium, large; normal medium), `soda` (cola, lemonLime, orangeSoda; normal cola),
`tea` (lemonade, icedTea; normal lemonade). The diner uses the Burger Bar's own picks (`from`, `of: 'size'`,
`of: 'flavour'`, `item.size`, `nameFrom: 'flavour'`), no slots; new packs use slots (pizza is the worked example).

**Combos** (level 3 up): an order is one item, or two at the level's `more` odds, of different courses: a burger with
fries, onion rings or a drink, or a side with a drink; never two burgers, except Gus's two of one thing. Listed main,
side, drink. Order Size "One Item" makes every order one item.

## 5. The ladder

`levels: {}`: the engine's numbers (pack-format.md 12) are the Burger Bar's.

| Level | On offer | Items | Gross-outs | Extras |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | hamburger, cheeseburger | 1; at most 2 optional toppings kept; change 0.2 | none | |
| 2 | + bacon cheeseburger, double cheeseburger, fries, onion rings | 1; longer tickets; change 0.3 | none | |
| 3 | + fountain drink, lemonade or iced tea | 1 or 2 (35% two); combos | 0.3 an order, at most 2 a shift, never the first | |
| 4 | + the Diner Tower | as 3, change 0.4 | as 3 | one ridiculous order at 50% a shift; one visitor (Reginald or Kai), never first |
| 5 | the same | as 4, change 0.5, fancy picks (extra crispy) | 0.35 an order, at most 2 | ridiculous orders at 60%, `bunInside` too |

## 6. Ridiculous orders (level 4 and 5)

The customer says `order.odd.<id>` instead of the order; the ticket is plain and complete (made with change 0, the
customer's dislikes still held). At most one a shift, never the first order or the visitor's. Anyone but a visitor.

| id | level | recipe | the change | The ticket | Presses |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `fivePatties` | 4 | `tower` | none: "five patties" is said, the line makes three | The Diner Tower: three patties, medium, with cheese, bacon, lettuce, tomato, pickles, onion, ketchup, mustard and mayo | 14 |
| `nothingGreen` | 4 | `baconCheeseburger` | holds lettuce, pickles; adds mustard, mayo | Bacon Cheeseburger: one patty, medium, with cheese, bacon, tomato, onion, ketchup, mustard and mayo | 13 |
| `bunInside` | 5 | `cheeseburger` | none: the bun on the inside is said, never made (spec 2.3; the proposal's third) | Cheeseburger: one patty, medium, with cheese, lettuce, tomato, pickles and ketchup | 13 |

## 7. The five-star event: The Burger Eating Contest

```js
events: { five: { name: 'The Burger Eating Contest', customers: ['gus', 'sal', 'dale', 'vernon', 'marge', 'oakes'],
  finale: { customer: 'bev', items: [{ recipe: 'teamStack', set: { doneness: 'well' } }] } } }
```

- Shift Length orders at level-4 complexity (level 4's recipes, items [1, 2], gross-outs), no visitors, no odd orders.
- The contestants order in rounds (everyone once before anyone twice). Coach Bev is the finale only: she orders for
  her team, who are spoken of, never shown (her `order.gag` "for the team" lines, diner-script's).
- The finale ticket: "The Team Stack: three patties, well done, with cheese, pickles, onion, ketchup and mustard." It
  is drawn giant (1.6 times, capped at 1.2 on the board by the set's `giantMax`) and adds no choices: 14 presses.
- If Bev isn't drawn, the first drawn regular (Marge) orders it. Mitch: `event.intro`, `event.celebrate`, `event.again`.

## 8. Who comes in, and what they order

Persona fields (name, pictures, voice, traits) are the cast's. Only drawn people come in (`BBCast.drawn`).

| id | role | likes (weight; others 0.5, rare 0.1) | also | The Burger Bar's design |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `marge` | regular | cheeseburger 3, hamburger 1 | `usual`: cheeseburger, medium (always, at every level; she says `order.usual`) | "The usual, hon" |
| `gus` | regular | cheeseburger 2, bacon cheeseburger 2, hamburger 1 | cast `twin`: from level 3 always two of one thing (`order.twin`); tipScale 1.25 | "One for now, one for the road" |
| `bev` | regular | double 3, bacon 2, Tower 1 | `favourite`: double cheeseburger, +2 tip (`react.favourite`); the event's finale | double, protein |
| `vernon` | regular | cheeseburger 3, hamburger 2, double 1 | cast `exact` (strays at change 0.5 or more), threeStarScale 1.5 | very exact orders |
| `sal` | regular | bacon 3, double 2, cheeseburger 1, Tower 1 | `dislikes: ['lettuce']` (held on every burger; `order.dislike`); `favourite`: bacon cheeseburger, +2 | never lettuce |
| `dale` | regular | onion rings 4, cheeseburger 1 | `always: ['onionRings']` (from level 2), `set: { fry: 'extraCrispy' }`, `favourite`: onion rings, +2 | the onion-ring guy, extra crispy |
| `oakes` | regular | lemonade 3, hamburger 1 | `set: { tea: 'lemonade' }`, `dislikes: ['onion']` (held on the bacon, double and Tower; never added). He can still order Onion Rings at weight 0.5: the rings are the recipe's item, not a part, and `O.canOrder` looks only at parts (asked of orders.js's owner) | lemonade, hates onions |
| `reginald` | visitor, level 4 | cheeseburger 1 | cast `newest`: always the Diner Tower (the newest recipe on offer at 4 and 5), plus a side or drink as the level allows | the critic |
| `kai` | visitor, level 4 | hamburger 2, cheeseburger 2 | cast `short` (one item); `set: { cupSize: 'small' }` | a small burger, a small drink |

New against the old pack (from DESIGN.md's cast table, no presses added): Dale's extra crispy, Oakes's lemonade, Kai's
small cup. Gone from the Burger Bar (spec 5.4): Priya (the Cafe's), Tasha (Smoothie Shack and Ice Cream Emporium).
Marge keeps a one-item usual: a two-item usual (cheeseburger and iced tea) would set her item count, which only the
level may do (spec 0.6). The tutorial customer and the first-drawn stand-in is Marge (first in the list).

