| `ice` | `ice` | | cubes; waits in a scoop |
| `cola`, `lemonLime`, `orangeSoda`, `lemonade`, `icedTea` | `drink` | colour #4a2412, #d9f2a0, #ff8a1c, #fff07a, #9a5a1e | poured from the fountain into the cup |
| recipe `teamStack` | `look: { giant: true }` | | the whole burger 1.6 times bigger |

Sets: `counter` (fixed camera), `grill` (cook `grill`), `board`, `fryer` (cook `fryer`), `drinks` (its `pick` hook
drops the cup, then pours). No auto steps, no slot looks, no Requests for new looks.

## 11. Sounds

Station hooks (audio.md 5.2): grill `cook: 'sizzle'` (the patties go on the heat), `done: 'flip'`; fryer `cook:
'fryer'`, `add: 'salt'` (its only Add); drinks `done: 'fountain'` (the drink is its last step; timing: section 18).
Defaults elsewhere: every other Add plays `plop`, each Timed stage `tick`; the board's sauces `squirt`. The page plays
`swoosh` (Skip), `toss` (Swap It), `buzz` (fly), `ding`, `kaching`, `stars`, `ew` as before. All in `packs/diner/sound`
or `packs/shared/sound`.

## 12. The script (packs/diner/script.js)

This pass changed only what the format forces: `plainIds: true` (every diner clip keeps today's id, e.g.
`vernon/extra.1.pickles`, `mitch/cook`), and Mitch's line `cook` moved from moment `tutorial.cook` to
`tutorial.cook.grill`. All 145 lines keep their text and id. `SC.check` on the merged script: no problems.

diner-script (the same day) wrote the rest: 179 new lines (324 in all), every moment covered for every speaker who
comes here, `format: 3` on the pack, and `BB_PACKS=diner node --test "tests/script.test.cjs"` passes. The script in
words (who has what, the conventions the other packs copy, what the page does with each moment, the clip list for
the voice pass) is `docs/api/packs/diner-script.md`. Bev's "for the team" is her `order.gag` (see section 18).

## 13. Help

"Follow the ticket: add what is on it and skip what is not. At the grill, add one patty for each on the ticket, then
choose how done. At the board, the toppings and sauces come down the line one at a time, and the buns go on by
themselves. From two stars, the fryer makes fries and onion rings: pick which, choose how crispy, then salt them or
skip the salt. From three stars, a burger can come with a side or a drink; at the drinks station, pick the cup size,
add ice or skip it, then pick the drink. If something looks nasty, choose Swap It for a fresh one. With Timed cooking,
take the food off when it reaches what the ticket says. At the end, check the order, redo anything that is wrong,
then ring it up."

