| wheelInk, wheelSteel, wheelDark | #1b120e, #d6dce1, #9aa4ad | the ticket wheel |

Contrast, measured: the highlight (#ffd400) is 10:1 on pageBg and well over 3:1 on the boards, but only about 1.1:1 on
panelTop and 2.1:1 on panelBottom, where today's Burger Bar relies on the highlight's thickness, glow and lift. A new
palette should keep its panel darker or lighter than that, not copy it.

## 15. The tutorial

Marge; one Bacon Cheeseburger, medium, no onions: "Bacon Cheeseburger: one patty, medium, with cheese, bacon,
lettuce, tomato and ketchup." The cheese comes down mouldy (`gross: { item: 0, ing: 'cheese', event: 'mouldy' }`).
Always Simple; Mitch warns before each mistake. 13 presses done right, plus one Swap It.

## 16. Press counts (`pressReport('diner')`, Serve included; Simple and Timed alike, the same at every level)

| recipe | levels | presses |
|---|---|---|
| hamburger, cheeseburger | 1-5 | 13 (grill 3: Add, Done, a stage; board 9; Serve) |
| baconCheeseburger | 2-5 | 13 |
| doubleCheeseburger | 2-5 | 14 (grill 4: Add, Add, Done, a stage) |
| fries, onionRings | 2-5 | 4 (pick, stage, salt, Serve) |
| fountain, lemonade | 3-5 | 4 (size, ice, drink, Serve) |
| tower | 4-5 | 14 |
| teamStack (event) | event | 14 |

Whole orders (bots, 25 shifts a level, both modes): level 1 at most 13; level 2 at most 14; levels 3-5 at most 27
(Gus's two doubles: 13 + 13 + Serve); the event 28 (two doubles and a Swap It). The ceiling is 28: two three-patty
burgers and one Swap It. Budget (spec 4.3): level 1 ≤ 14, any order ≤ 28.

## 17. What changed for the player (against the live Burger Bar)

- Orders follow the restaurant's stars, not the old Orders setting: at 1 star one hamburger or cheeseburger with at
  most two optional toppings; the bacon and double cheeseburgers, fries and onion rings at 2; combos with drinks at 3;
  the Tower at 4. (The live game offered every burger from the start, never the fryer or drinks, and up to two items.)
- Gross-outs start at 3 stars (they came from the first shift); ridiculous orders and visitors at 4; the Burger Eating
  Contest when the fifth star is due.
- The grill's question is "How done?" (was "Cook the patty. How done?") and Timed's prompt "Take it off when it is
  right." (was "The patty is cooking. Take it off when it is right."): every stage set now names its words.
- Dale, Professor Oakes, Reginald and Kai come in once their pictures are drawn; Priya and Tasha no longer come here.
- Unchanged: every recipe, ingredient, look, ticket word, price, gross-out, the tutorial, and every line and clip id.

## 18. For the page (page-1)

Read the merged pack only (`BB.cast.merge(BBCast, BBPacks.diner)`): `poses`, the manager's name and voice and every
customer's name, art and voice come from the cast; Mitch's pictures are `packs/cast/art/cast/mitch-burger/`. Create
shifts with `level` (and `drawn`): there are no `orderStyles` now, so a shift without a level falls back to one
plain item. Each scene's picture is its station's `backdrop` (`pack.backdrops` is gone). Draw the Timed tools by name
(`spatula`, `fryerBasket`, both in `packs/shared/art/props`; a drawn button when there is no prop), apply `theme`, read `help` for Pause > Help, and play
station sounds by hook. The drinks station's `done` (the fountain) belongs with the pour, which the drinks set starts
on the flavour pick (`onApply`); `phaseDone` comes in the same batch of events. `order.gag` is required only of locals
at home, but Coach Bev's "for the team" is hers: say a customer's own `order.gag` line after the order whenever they
have one (at least on the event's finale), or her team is never mentioned.

## 19. Copying this for another restaurant

Keep the order of fields and their comments. Change: id, version 1, name, help, theme (your palette; check contrast),
courses, stage sets (with ask and stop, at least 12/8/5 s and ×2), ingredients and looks (only your food module's),
slots and picks, stations (backdrop, redo words, tool, sounds), recipes (level, course, price), `levels` only where you
differ, gross-outs (Add steps or picks of ≤ 3 values), `manager.art`, regulars (spec 5.4, ids only plus what they
order), `oddOrders`, `events.five` (a giant `level: 'event'` recipe if the brief has one), `tutorial`. Leave out
`format` until the script is complete. Then run the checks at the top and report `pressReport`.
